WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.449
- Uh, Ch..

00:00:03.205 --> 00:00:06.547
(Welsh country music)

00:00:08.186 --> 00:00:10.391
- I had no idea that they had
their own language (laughs)

00:00:10.391 --> 00:00:12.121
- Aren't like all the royalty

00:00:12.121 --> 00:00:13.967
princes and princesses of Wales?

00:00:14.259 --> 00:00:15.604
- [Voiceover] Tywyn

00:00:15.604 --> 00:00:17.531
- Honestly looks to me like a little baby

00:00:17.531 --> 00:00:18.851
just got mad at the keyboard.

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:19.946
It went like this.

00:00:19.946 --> 00:00:21.664
- Tywin, that's how you spell
Tywin Lannister, isn't it?

00:00:21.664 --> 00:00:22.546
- Tun?

00:00:22.546 --> 00:00:25.008
- Taiwan! No, it's not Taiwan.

00:00:25.008 --> 00:00:26.784
- Tywyn (bell rings)

00:00:26.784 --> 00:00:29.628
(gasps) Oh my God!

00:00:29.628 --> 00:00:32.682
- Why do the two "y"'s
make different noises?

00:00:32.682 --> 00:00:34.121
- [Voiceover] Crymych

00:00:34.121 --> 00:00:36.721
- This looks like a game
of Hangman that I lost.

00:00:36.721 --> 00:00:38.184
Right? Like there are a bunch of dashes

00:00:38.184 --> 00:00:39.403
and I just didn't get the vowels.

00:00:39.403 --> 00:00:40.704
- Do ya cry much?

00:00:40.704 --> 00:00:43.130
That looks like an advertisement
for an anti-depressant.

00:00:43.131 --> 00:00:44.621
- Searmych?

00:00:44.621 --> 00:00:47.806
- The accent is key. Creimooch.

00:00:47.806 --> 00:00:49.907
- So the "y" is an "uh"...

00:00:49.907 --> 00:00:51.823
- I think I could mess with this language.

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:53.587
- [Voiceover] Ynysybwl

00:00:53.587 --> 00:00:55.805
- What?! What is that?

00:00:55.805 --> 00:00:57.279
- (laughs)

00:00:57.279 --> 00:00:58.472
- That looks like a rapper's name.

00:00:58.472 --> 00:00:59.961
Like Young Souble.

00:00:59.961 --> 00:01:02.039
- Yessebellme.

00:01:02.039 --> 00:01:03.061
- Enisebul

00:01:03.061 --> 00:01:04.164
- Nice Boy.

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:05.545
- [Voiceover] Ynysybwl.

00:01:05.545 --> 00:01:06.625
- Okay.

00:01:06.625 --> 00:01:07.713
- Sounds like what you
say when you're cold.

00:01:07.713 --> 00:01:09.957
You're just like "Brrr." Ynysybrrrr.

00:01:11.141 --> 00:01:12.785
- [Voiceover] Ysbyty Ystwyth

00:01:12.785 --> 00:01:14.906
- The top looks like a dumb start-up

00:01:14.906 --> 00:01:16.392
that you'd see in Silicon Valley.

00:01:16.392 --> 00:01:17.565
- Eyes-beady-vigith?

00:01:18.457 --> 00:01:19.585
- Wobydy Wosidey.

00:01:19.585 --> 00:01:22.173
- Ispitty Istwith.

00:01:22.173 --> 00:01:23.590
- [Voiceover] Ysbyty Ystwyth

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:27.873
- What? I'm sorry, what?

00:01:27.873 --> 00:01:31.345
- That's so cool! This
is the coolest language.

00:01:33.281 --> 00:01:36.024
- [Voiceover]
LLanfairpwllgwyngyllgogerychwyrndrobwylll-

00:01:36.024 --> 00:01:38.376
lantysiliogogogoch

00:01:38.376 --> 00:01:39.667
- (screams)

00:01:39.728 --> 00:01:42.931
- Yeah, no, I'm just
gonna go. I'm just done.

00:01:42.931 --> 00:01:44.603
- (laughs)

00:01:44.603 --> 00:01:47.471
- This is one word?

00:01:47.471 --> 00:01:49.293
- Were they drunk when
they named this town?

00:01:49.293 --> 00:01:49.990
This is a town?

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:54.123
- Lahnfairpwhygwangwyelgogurch

00:01:54.123 --> 00:01:58.511
- Sherwindrabbellalalalantisigiggugugoch.

00:01:59.202 --> 00:02:00.589
Nailed it!

00:02:00.589 --> 00:02:02.470
- [voiceover] LLanfairpwllgwyngyll-

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:04.745
gogerychwyrndrobwyllllantysiliogogogoch

00:02:04.745 --> 00:02:08.205
- (laughs) What?! No!

00:02:08.205 --> 00:02:10.190
- That sounds like you're making this up.

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:12.710
- It sounds like an ancient
prayer, more than a town.

00:02:12.710 --> 00:02:16.246
- I think Welsh people value city names.

00:02:16.708 --> 00:02:19.246
I think in America it's
kind of an after-thought.

00:02:19.246 --> 00:02:20.685
- I still want to go to Wales,

00:02:20.685 --> 00:02:24.981
'cause it's beautiful, I hear.

00:02:24.981 --> 00:02:28.487
I don't wanna ever have to
follow directions there.

00:02:28.487 --> 00:02:31.645
- It's very interesting that
it's so close to England

00:02:31.645 --> 00:02:34.825
and we associate it
with being like England

00:02:34.825 --> 00:02:37.859
but it's so very different.

